Example circuits
================

Open one, press Resolve (F8) and look at the Result panel; the Plot links
there show the frequency response.

rc-lowpass-2nd-order.info
  Two cascaded RC low-pass sections (R = 1 kOhm, C = 1 uF).
  Result:  V1 / (C1 C2 R1 R2 s^2 + (C2 R2 + C1 R1 + C2 R1) s + 1),
  poles near -381.97 and -2618.03 rad/s.

rlc-bandpass.info
  Series RLC band-pass, output across R (L = 10 mH, C = 1 uF, R = 100 Ohm:
  centre frequency about 1.59 kHz, Q = 1).
  Result:  C1 R1 V1 s / (C1 L1 s^2 + C1 R1 s + 1).

opamp-inverting.info
  Inverting amplifier with an ideal op-amp (R1 = 1 kOhm, R2 = 10 kOhm).
  Result:  -R2 V1 / R1 (gain -10).

sallen-key-lowpass.info
  Unity-gain Sallen-Key low-pass (R1 = R2 = 10 kOhm, C1 = 20 nF,
  C2 = 10 nF: Butterworth, cut-off about 1.13 kHz).
  Result:  V1 / (C1 C2 R1 R2 s^2 + (C2 R2 + C2 R1) s + 1).
